From 57a2d639c7ef02929dfdc07095496b6b9fd8819d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:30:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] feat(media): detect changing burned-in caption bands

Add backend/src/media/burned_captions.py, an OpenCV + NumPy detector for
source subtitles that are already in the picture. It samples frames,
scans each one with a sliding horizontal strip, and keeps only wide,
glyph-rich strips that hold outlined bright strokes and spike in edge
density against the equal-size strips just above and below them. This
finds a subtitle that touches other scene edges, which a connected-box
scan does not.

Candidates are clustered by vertical centre across the samples. A
cluster becomes a CaptionBand only when it appears in at least 35% of
the samples and its fixed-rectangle stroke mask changes between frames
(Jaccard distance), so static channel names, "follow us" panels, logos,
no-text footage and busy textures are rejected. The band is returned in
source pixels with confidence and the sample counts.

Add synthetic ffmpeg drawtext tests for changing bottom and top bands,
static text in one and both bands, no text, a noisy texture, and a
static tag over moving video; add tools/burned-captions-proof/run_proof.py,
which runs the detector over the four phase-2 sources, times it, and
saves one outlined debug frame per source.

Attribution: OpenCode (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free), lane-b/round2.
